ed  where the dendritic cell precursors are  being generated  and matured at some point a tumor  antigen loading process  is happening where the vaccine product  is prepared  and infused back into the patient with  hopes  of sharing this tumor antigen  presentation knowledge with the t cells  so in our case we engineered  adenovirally transduced vaccines  with three shared melanoma antigens by  rosinase smart one and may g6  so vaccines are usually safe but the  question is are they effective  there's about 200 dendritic cell  clinical trials  or more today but the efficacy of the  dendritic cell vaccines is still  questionable  in terms of our clinical trial here's a  brief summary of it a a schematic  diagram  where here at the baseline day zero  prior to that  first set of leukophoresis has been  conducted  where the vaccine product have been  generated  that is then being infused three times  into the patients  and the day 43 second set of  lycophoresis is generated  then actually patients are being divided  into two branches  with or without high-dose interference  alpha treatment  and dayday 89 then concluding over the  trial has a  another locophoresis so you can see we  have three different time points for  analysis  and there has been a wealth of molecular  and clinical data  coming out of this trial we've used  numerous things  like a cytokine cytokine serum profiling  molecular profiling of the circulating  lymphocytes  and a lot of immuno monitoring of the  lymphocytes of these patients  including tumor biopsies  so going on here just to show you a  quick quick  responses in the trial where we see some  partial responders  uh and uh of course some early  progressors unfortunately  and then we have also some no evidence  of disease patients  that were actually separated into good  and them categories  based on their time of progression so  good and bad outcomes  those are the two categories i will  refer to  so the study objective of our trial  or or or actually the study work was to  analyze  the cancer patient-specific t-cell  responses  so i'm going to go ahead and to show you  that to confirm  that the dendritic cell vaccines induced  and activated a successful  tumor-specific  responses we conducted alispot assays  from total pbmc cultures  and this demonstrated that majority of  patients showed actually increased in  interferon gamma producing t  cells in response to the antigens and  that indicated successful vaccination  now the closer look at the baseline  responses shown at the bottom there  show that about half of the patient  showed pre-existing  functional pistol responses to the  melanoma antigens  prior to vaccination but  there were no associations between  having these pre-existing responses  and t-cell responses and some sort of  favorable outcome  next because 16 patients were hlhd  positive  they were able to use eczema to measure  the pistol frequencies  and identify peptide specific cd8 pistol  responses  so on the left hand side here you can  see changes in the cd8 frequencies at  multiple time points  starting from baseline continuing post  and these are further broken down here  in the middle diagrams  by patient response and the take-home  message here is that we did not see  any consistent trend in patient-cda  t-cell tumor antigen reactivity  among these groups after vaccination  and as with the trend observing the ali  spot data  the majority of 16 patients here had  dextromer positive  cells at baseline but again this did not  set a stage for a better clinical  outcomes for the patients  so collectively so we saw that the  responses to individual antigens  did not seem significantly impact  clinical outcome  but what we did we actually took all the  individual responses  and uh to all three shared antigens and  group them into a one combined response  and what we were able to see here based  on these kepler kepler-meyer plots  is that a vaccine in the ucda t-cell  response  showed significant association with  overall progression-free survival  with overall survival and  progression-free survival uh so going on  the uh then we're interested a little  bit more  into a effect of a previous checkpoint  blockade  uh blockade for these patients so  because um  many of these patients were in late  stage disease  they they often had previous uh  therapies  and uh here we subdivided the patients  based on uh  receiving either antiped1 or and or  ctlx4  and what we saw here was that uh tcl  responses overall  were higher in patients that had  previously received  one of the checkpoint blockades  therapies and here i'm first showing  dextromer frequencies  that show a small but significant  difference based on the  previous therapy for uh may j6  specifically  and going on uh here i'm showing a  uh frequency external frequency  responses  and uh what we see here is that  the only ma-specific diesel response  that showed  some sort of clear increase over time  was again h6  so um that that was quite an interesting  result and  it suggests that the previous blockade  of ctla4 or pd1 can slightly amplify  some of the ma-specific responses and  difference  this difference can persist through the  course of vaccination  uh all right going on next we were  also interested in profiling  the exhaustion molecules of these cells  and here i'm going to only share a pd-1  expression levels and uh what it was  interesting was to see that the best  responders the two patients that were pr  patients actually showed really really  uh extremely low levels of pd-1  on their ma-specific cd8 collections  uh the other uh exhaustion monitors did  not relate significantly with  any kind of clinical response so next we  use nanostring profiling to look at the  levels  and and really to deeply profile these  uh circulating lymphocytes  from these patients and here uh some  data for the protein counting data  for these checkpoint molecules uh pd1  and cp4  now uh what we saw is that in general  uh both of these molecules were elevated  their expression levels were elevated in  the bad outcome patients  at both measurements at both at the  baseline at  a43 so  we also analyzed this data by looking at  time dependent change and even though  this data didn't come statistically  significant  there were certainly at least for the  ctla-4 data we saw a  very close significance  in showing that the ctla4 or pd1  expression levels were higher in the bad  outcome patients  we've also used univariate cox  regression analysis  to kind of determine whether or not  their levels  at baseline or post-vaccine correlated  with  overall or progression-free survival and  indeed  uh many of these it  so we've used a pan-cancer immune  profiling panel  and cardi characterization panel in  order to better understand the pathways  and the gene expression profiles of  these  uh basically patient circulating  lymphocytes  and the way we've done this comparison  is it was based on outcome groups so we  separated the good and bad outcome  groups at both  baseline and post-vaccine treatments and  we saw certainly an interesting  signatures  or or different gene expression changes  and then we've looked at the pathway  analysis  what we saw was the following and again  just to position you  we have uh the red and blue denoted  pathways that are either upregulated or  down regulated  uh based on a clinical outcome  and broken down at baseline or day 43.  so what we saw is that a lot of  interesting pathways associated with  emptor signaling tcl receptor signaling  b-cell receptor signaling  where upper upper regulated in the in  the good outcome category  while strong uh type one interferon  response signatures  were associated with the with the worst  clinical prognosis  here is also shown that uh ctla-4  pathway  actually came up as a upregulated in the  bad outcome patients  now we've also correlated pathways with  overall and progression-free survival  and what was interesting was that we saw  the t-cell responses  were strongly correlative with overall  survival  and diesel responses with  progression-free survival  and we also saw that the interferon type  one signatures were  present in in in the low uh unfavorable  survival category now  lastly i'm going to share some data from  the two tumor biopsies  that are we are actually currently  investigating right now  where we actually applied several  nanostring uh sequencing panels to  and uh what we actually saw is uh and i  understand this is a little bit of a  complicated slide  and i just want you to focus your  attention on these different signatures  and what we actually saw is some  interesting uh hypoxia-like and  geogenesis  uh and vegeta associated signatures uh  that that actually were correlative of  bad clinical outcome  there are additional uh pathways like  integrin ecm  stromalite components stolage receptor  signaling pgf beta  again uh some consistent themes along  the  uh tumor micro environment now uh what  is interesting  is that the vegf interested us because  of some additional data that we have  collected including  blood serum cytokines and whatnot and  they've actually looked at a pathway  specifically related to these  in both three panels and what we saw  and it was really nice to see that there  were several genes that were  consistently  upregulated in the bad outcome patients  across the different panels so it was  sort of a external validation of the  data  so this is just kind of an example of  the pathways signatures that we see in  the bad outcome patients in the tumors  so collectively i would like to conclude  the talk  by by summarizing the data where we show  that a majority of our 35 patients were  successfully vaccinated  in this clinical trial and uh not  individual antigens but the combined  total  of tumor antigen-specific cd8 responses  were associated with  favorable overall progression in overall  survival  so that's that that argues for the  importance of diesel responses  in these spider vaccines and the  previous checkpoint therapy  enhanced some of the uh tumor-associated  uh antigen uh testosterone-specific  responses  uh and in some cases they uh continued  uh elevated over time  uh and the two patients with the best  clinical outcomes  certainly showed a very low pd-1  expression surface markers  uh analysis of pd-1 and ctla-4 protein  expression  uh using a protein counting nanostring  panel  uh in lymphocytes showed  increase in expression of these  checkpoint molecules  in the bad outcome patients and  what we saw is that a lot of high immune  checkpoint  type one is their fear and responses  t-cell exhaustion like gene expression  networks  were associated with uh with inferior  clinical outcome in patients  and lastly we're looking into the tumors  and so some interesting  uh like uh extracellular or  matrix stroma-like uh signatures that  associate it with inferior clinical  outcome in patients  so with that i'd like to thank uh my  mentor uh dr butterfield  and uh some of the people that  collectively helped with the work  uh of patty santos uh dina and paul  um our collaborators team halves  also from the parker institute he's in  the bioinformatics department he was  instrumental in helping with some of the  bioinformatic analyses  and also sarah warren from nanostring  from helping conducting  this nanostring sequencing research and  uh  this is a picture showing the parker  institute for cancer immunotherapy  that is where we are located and i'll be  happy to take  any questions  have you looked the whether blockade of  pd1 during  antigen presentation by dendritic cells  had any functional impact on the tumor  androgen specific t cells  so yes had uh actually engineered a  dendritic cells that were expressing  uh antipd-1 antibody and they were  co-curvatured together with with the  patient t cells and we did not see any  effect  of blockade of pd1 during the  the tumor antigen cross presentation so  uh we did not see benefit adding that uh  during the  post during the antigen presentation  however  we certainly suggest that there may be  additional mechanisms  or perhaps the blockade of the  checkpoints after the vaccination may  potentially increase the benefit of the  vaccine  did you measure the antigen expression  levels in dendritic cells  and if so did you see any correlations  between antigen expression levels  and t cell or clinical responses  so yes so we've looked at the levels of  antigen expression levels both in the  vaccines  i mean in the vaccines both by rna and  protein  and uh we did not see any correlations  between the amount of expression of  particular antigen  in the dendritic cells and better t cell  responses  so that was not apparent  did you observe any correlations between  cd4 and cd8 cell responses  so we looked at uh and actually a  reviewer asked us that  uh for our manuscript whether or not  there were any correlation between cd4  responses  so we have uh extensively analyzed cd4t  cells just like the cd80 cells  but we did not see a specific  correlation  in any way with the cd8 cells um to any  of the tumor antigens  so uh well we believe they're important  and you know many studies are coming out  of their impair importance in  immunotherapy treatments  we did not see a correlation between cd8  and cd4 t cell responses  to these shared tumor antigens  did you analyze insoluble serum  checkpoint molecules  so yes we have analyzed uh actually a  whole panel  of soluble checkpoint molecules uh  including  pd1 and ctla4 but many of those actually  did not come up  in terms of a good signal but uh what we  saw was a soluble expression of pdl2  uh as well as lag three and team three  showed some interesting correlations  with clinical outcome  and i'm going to point out soluble pdl2  that  showed a significant association  done by uh hazard ratio analysis as well  as uh  correlative analyses that the elevated  levels of pdl2 actually uh predicted a  better  outcome in patients now while we don't  know what it really  means there are some studies indicating  that pdl2 may have some  different and perhaps even activation  specific roles but  we don't understand what it means yet  but the clinical correlations were very  significant for pdl2  so i'd like to summarize the study uh by  saying that  uh while most of the patients were  significantly  um vaccinated uh in our clinical trial  uh individual tumor antigens were not  predictive of clinical response  the combined total was certainly  impactful  in terms of clinical outcome  such as overall survival and  progression-free survival responses  nanostring signature uh profiling uh  certainly demonstrated in  interesting uh patterns in in a  checkpoint molecule expression such as  pd1 ctla4  and we show a strong associations with  or their increase  uh strong associations with inferior  survival and patients  um i would like to thank everybody for  the attention  uh i'd like to thank again the  organizers for putting this event  together  uh and nanostring for uh sponsoring the  event and  thank you

